  "cohort_rules": [
    "Define the publisher portfolio and whether multiple game titles are eligible; exclude non-game assets unless separate report.",
    "Fix initial paid settlement date, retain partial/fully refunded distinctions, and treat reversals before counting a retained order.",
    "At 30/90/365 days report full follow-up, right-censored and lost-account records separately, never classify an unobservable later purchase as confirmed never-return.",
    "Distinct retained orders are not distinct buyers; deduplicate only with authorization in private seller-side environment, then release disclosure-safe aggregates.",
    "Exclude gifted keys, bundle claims, free downloads and merely activated Patreon entitlements from second paid orders.",
    "Do not use marketing source or follower conversion without aligned campaign cohorts and a defensible comparison.",
    "Measure external Patreon renewal/churn using that platform's own data and term lengths; never infer this from itch.io key issuance or revocation.",
    "For churn, define cancellation effective at paid-period end and grace period, not the date a cancellation action was requested.",
    "Segment first-time vs multi-title past customers with pre-cohort purchases when permitted; if historic coverage incomplete declare left-censoring.",
    "Report attribution, customer privacy, commercial paid order eligibility, period, refund basis, fees, country and selection bias."
  ],
